From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 04:25:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: clean vkd3d-proton's transfer destinations in cached
 memory when recorded

vkd3d-proton zero-fills every new host-visible allocation, suballocations
included, with a CPU memset that it never flushes. It puts READBACK heaps
in PanVK's non-coherent cached memory type, where those dirty zero lines
later land over what the GPU wrote, either on eviction or through the
clean+invalidate that vkInvalidateMappedMemoryRanges does. Readbacks then
come back zero in 64-byte runs: 144 of the 153 failures in vkd3d-proton
2.14.1's test suite. With VKD3D_CONFIG=memory_allocator_skip_clear the
buffer readback tests pass 30/30 on the device, so the memset is the cause.

D3D12 creates a resource, memset included, before any command can use it,
and READBACK resources can only be copy destinations. So when a fill,
update, buffer copy, image-to-buffer copy or query result copy is recorded
into non-coherent cached memory that is mapped, the destination range's CPU
cache lines are cleaned there. The cost is proportional to the bytes
copied, paid once per recorded command. Buffers now remember the memory
they are bound to, and the mapping of such memory changes under the
emulated-coherent lock so the clean can't race an unmap.

Making the type driver-coherent for vkd3d (rg477m/016) also fixes it, but
cleans every mapped 16 MiB chunk on every submission: -8% in Serious Sam's
D3D12 renderer. Hiding the cached type isn't possible: vkd3d-proton then
fails READBACK allocations with E_OUTOFMEMORY.

Not covered: textures that vkd3d reads and writes on the CPU
(WriteToSubresource/ReadFromSubresource), which it never flushes.

On by default for engine "vkd3d" only; PANVK_CLEAN_XFER_DST=0/1 turns it
off/on for any engine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: D3D12 correctness: vkd3d-proton readbacks no longer come back zero in 64-byte runs (its unflushed CPU memset of new READBACK/CUSTOM allocations in the non-coherent cached type landed over GPU results); transfer destinations in mapped non-coherent cached memory get their CPU cache lines cleaned when the transfer is recorded; engine "vkd3d" only, PANVK_CLEAN_XFER_DST=0/1 overrides
Upstream-commit: none
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: rg477m/016 (emulated-coherent lock and sync helpers); applies after rg477m/041
Validation test: vkd3d-proton 2.14.1 test suite on the device, 4 readback tests x 10 interleaved runs: buffer readbacks 30/30 pass (rg477m/041 build: 4/30; VKD3D_CONFIG=memory_allocator_skip_clear on 041: 30/30, so the memset is the cause), texture CPU readback (test_read_write_subresource_2d) still fails as before; PanProbe 38/38 x2; Serious Sam Fusion D3D12 renderer bot benchmark uncapped, quietd Stock, A-B-B-A x2: 63.7 vs 63.5 fps (the driver-coherent alternative cost 8%); full suite (414 tests, runner v2 with crash retries) 121 -> 289 PASS: 167 FAIL->PASS, 1 CRASH->PASS, 2 FAIL->SKIP (stop at a feature check after their readback now works), none worse; DXVK games unchanged (engine-gated): Hades renders, Jupiter Hell tutorial 47.5 fps, Serious Sam D3D11 58.9 fps
Channel: compatibility, unsafe
